# A short Xbox Elite Series 2 evdev session, wired (`xpad`, 045e:0b00).
#
# Format: `type code value`, decimal or 0x-hex — the three numbers `evtest`
# prints per line, in the order the kernel emitted them. Blank lines and
# everything after a `#` are ignored, so a real capture pasted in here works
# unchanged. Recorded read-only; every line below is a synthetic stand-in with
# the shape and ordering the driver actually produces (one `SYN_REPORT`
# terminating each report, state changes only).
#
# 1 = EV_KEY, 3 = EV_ABS, 0 = EV_SYN (code 0 = SYN_REPORT).

# --- D-pad up, as a hat axis (xpad does not set MAP_DPAD_TO_BUTTONS here) ---
3 0x11 -1              # ABS_HAT0Y = -1
0 0 0

# --- the Xbox button down: the guide layer opens -----------------------------
1 0x13c 1              # BTN_MODE
0 0 0

# --- P1, the upper-right paddle, chorded under the guide ---------------------
1 0x225 1              # BTN_GRIPR
0 0 0

# --- both released in one report ---------------------------------------------
1 0x225 0
1 0x13c 0
3 0x11 0
0 0 0

# --- right trigger pulled past the 85 % full-pull threshold -------------------
3 0x05 900             # ABS_RZ, 900/1023 = 0.88
0 0 0

# --- right stick to the upper right (evdev +Y is down, so up is negative) -----
3 0x03 24000           # ABS_RX
3 0x04 -24000          # ABS_RY
0 0 0
